# A deployment's own configuration. The templates are generated from the parser
# and committed, so a reader on GitHub sees every setting; the filled-in files
# are this host's and never leave it.
*.toml
!*.toml.example
!.gitignore

# What `kbconfig upgrade` keeps of the file it replaced. The same host's
# configuration under another name, and `*.toml` above does not match it.
*.toml.bak

# `kbconfig schema configs` writes an editor's view of the same structs: the
# documents into schema/, and the .taplo.toml above that maps one to each file.
# This host's copy of something the binary already carries, and worth no diff.
/schema/
